# Assets are model-facing content, and their exact bytes are the deliverable rather
# than a style choice. The pr skill's output contract depends on precise fence widths
# and indentation, and reflowing an instruction fragment changes what a model reads,
# which is a behaviour change wearing a formatting change's clothes.
#
# Also practical: the installer symlinks a personal asset only when the emitted file
# is byte-identical to its source, so a formatter reaching in here can quietly turn
# links into copies.
#
# Format these by hand. If you do want Prettier on them, run `prettier --check` on
# one first and read the diff before committing to it.
